  "term": "alcoholism",
  "definition": "Alcoholism is a long-lasting disease shaped by inherited, psychological, social, and environmental influences. It commonly worsens over time and can be life-threatening, marked by loss of control over alcohol use, persistent focus on drinking, continued drinking despite harm, and impaired judgment such as denial; these problems may be ongoing or recur in periods.",
